-- title:
--   Places over a supersingular point: node or residue disc (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=3$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and a level guard is fixed: a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$.
--
--   **Base valuation ring and the supersingular point.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, that is $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. $W$ is a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A, M')$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$ — here $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(K,N)$ is the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ K$ generated over $K$ by the $q$-expansion `jqModC K` of $j$ and its $N$-fold expansion `jqNModC K N`, and a place is a valuation subring containing the constants, different from the whole field and with principal ideals. The hypothesis `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: those $w$ which are rational (the constants surject onto the residue field of $w$), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and for which $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the generator `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`. An element $s\in W$ is fixed.
--
--   **Fields of modular functions.** $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change `laurentBaseChange` of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\ M'$, the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \mathbb{Q}$ generated by the expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ d\ (\mathtt{jq})$ for $d\mid M'$; and $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H=\mathrm{levelH}\ q\ M'$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The hypothesis `hle` is the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$.
--
--   **Constant reduction.** $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A, M')$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose intersection with the constants is $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$ on constants, together with a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with orders of functions with nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $A\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$.
--
--   **Descent data over a discretely valued subfield.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lies in $A$; the valuation ring $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is assumed to be a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, Henselian, and with algebraically closed residue field; `hκ` requires every $a\in A$ to be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c\in k_0$ lying in $A$. Further auxiliary data: a prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and an element $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $K_b=\bot$ (so $K_b$ is $k_0$ itself), $A_b$ is the valuation subring of $K_b$ consisting of the elements lying in $A$, and $\varpi_b\ne 0$ generates the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for the $k_0$-algebra structure on $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ obtained by composing $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with the structure map of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$, and quantifies over the following further data, grouped as follows.
--
--   *(Form and its valuation ring.)* An intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ and a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is all of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$; for $x\in k_0$ one has $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$; $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal; and a linear disjointness condition: for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which is $K'$-linearly independent and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$.
--
--   *(Affine chart $B$.)* A subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ together with an $A_b$-algebra structure `alg` on $B$ such that: the structure map sends $a\in A_b$ to the image of $a$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$; $B$ is contained in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$, and that compositum is the field of fractions of $B$ (every element is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\ne 0$); $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; the quotient $B/(\varpi_b)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime; $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ away from $\varpi_b$, i.e. $f\in W_0$ if and only if $f\cdot h=g$ for some $g,h\in B$ with $\varpi_b\nmid h$; the image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ of the $q$-expansion `jq` of $j$ lies in $B$; and $B$ is stable under the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta\ \gamma$ for $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (an element of $\mathrm{Idx}\ q$) and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   *(Special fibre of $B$ as a Drinfeld quotient.)* For every $\mathrm{GaloisField}\ q\ 2$-algebra structure on $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$, assuming $\mathrm{CoordRing}\ q\ (\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A)$ is a domain, and for every $\zeta\in\mathrm{Idx}\ q$, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathrm{GaloisField}\ q\ 2$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to the fixed field $\mathrm{quotField}\ q\ (\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A)\ C_s$ inside the Drinfeld function field, such that $\#C_s=2\cdot\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\ q\ M'\ s$ (the width $\mathrm{jWidthChar}\ q$ of the $j$-value of $s$, which for $q=3$ is $6$ at $j=0$ and $1$ otherwise, divided by the ramification index $\mathrm{placeRamificationJ}\ M'\ s$); $\ker\rho=(\varpi_b)$; $\rho$ agrees on $A_b$ with the reduction $A\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$ followed by the structure map; every element of the quotient field is a ratio $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g,h\in B$, $\rho h\ne0$; the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those elements whose image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\ q\ (\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A)$; and $\rho$ is equivariant: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\ q\ \gamma,1)$ in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\ q$ and $f\in B$ with $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta\ \gamma^{-1}f\in B$, the image of $\rho(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta\ \gamma^{-1}f)$ in the Drinfeld function field is obtained from that of $\rho(f)$ by $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}$ at $(\mathrm{redQ}\ q\ \gamma,1)$.
--
--   *(Rationality.)* Every $f\in\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ whose underlying Laurent series lies in the image of $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\ \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, i.e. has rational coefficients, lies in $F_0$.
--
--   *(Nodes and the valuative cover over $s$.)* A finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ with the following property: for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ such that (i) for $x\in k_0$ one has $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $V$, and (ii) $V$ lies over $s$ in the sense that for every $g\in\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\ M'$ whose base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, has nonnegative order at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which the base change of `jq` has nonnegative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $g$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ lies in $F_0$, the resulting element lies in $V$, and for every $c\in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that element and the image of $c$ lies in $V$ and in the maximal ideal of $V$ — then either every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$, or there is $O\in\mathrm{nodes}$ with $O\subseteq V$ and such that every nonunit of $O$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   *(Regular prolongation, ends, base-smooth point stalks and discs.)* A field $FSS$ with a $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$-algebra structure and a `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ to $FSS$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ meeting the constants in $A$, with surjective residue map of kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero element can be scaled by a constant into $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue), such that for $f\in F_0$ one has $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $f\in W_0$. Further, a finite set $N$ of places of $FSS$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$, an assignment $Q\mapsto S_b(Q)$ of subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_b(Q):A_b[X]\to S_b(Q)$, ring homomorphisms $\chi_b(Q):S_b(Q)\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$, and sets $D_b(Q)$ of places of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, subject to one long conjunction, whose clauses are: $\#N=q+1$; $Q\notin N$ if and only if the $R$-residue of every element of $B$ lying in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$; for each $Q\notin N$ a package (summarised here) asserting that the images of $A_b$ lie in $S_b(Q)$ and are computed by $\varphi_b(Q)$ on constants, that $\chi_b(Q)$ reduces constants to $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$ and kills $\varphi_b(Q)X$, that $S_b(Q)$ is local with maximal ideal $\ker\chi_b(Q)$, that $S_b(Q)$ lies in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$ and has that compositum as field of fractions, that $\varphi_b(Q)$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type, that $S_b(Q)\subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $f$ in the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when $\varphi_b(Q)(\varpi_b)\mid f$, that the $R$-residue of each $f\in S_b(Q)$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and reduces there to the image of $\chi_b(Q)f$, that the $R$-residue of $\varphi_b(Q)X$ has $Q$-order $1$, that $B\subseteq S_b(Q)$ and $S_b(Q)$ is the localisation of $B$ at $Q$ (an element is in $S_b(Q)$ exactly when it is $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and the $R$-residue of $h$ a unit at $Q$), and that $D_b(Q)$ consists precisely of the rational places $P$ at which every $f\in S_b(Q)$ is regular with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in A$, and for which $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ is $<1$ exactly when $\chi_b(Q)f=0$; that the discs are pairwise disjoint, i.e. $P\in D_b(Q)\cap D_b(Q')$ with $Q,Q'\notin N$ forces $Q=Q'$; that for $Q\notin N$ and $P\in D_b(Q)$ the order of the image of `jq` at $P$ is nonnegative; and that for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta\ \gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and every place $Q$, one has $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q\in N$ if and only if $Q\in N$, and for $Q\notin N$ the translate $\{P:\tau^{-1}\cdot P\in D_b(Q)\}$ equals $D_b(R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under all of the above, for every place $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which is rational and which lies over $s$ in the following sense — for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ having nonnegative order at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ at which the base change of `jq` has nonnegative order and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ minus $a$ lies in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$ — at least one of the following holds:
--
--   1. there is $O\in\mathrm{nodes}$ such that every $f\in O$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$, and for every $f\in O$ which is not a unit of $O$ the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ lies in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$ (so $P$ dominates the node ring $O$); or
--
--   2. there is a place $Q$ of $FSS$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$ with $Q\notin N$ and $P\in D_b(Q)$.
--
--   This is the $q=3$ case, under the rigid level guard provided by the prime $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the step which transports the valuative covering statement over a supersingular point $s$ from valuation rings of the $k_0$-form $F_0$ to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-rational places of the geometric modular function field: such a place either dominates one of the finitely many node rings or lies in the residue disc of a smooth point of the special fibre outside the $q+1$ ends. It feeds the assembly of the semistable covering of the special fibre at supersingular points, being cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
